CAMERA LAW
FPV / cockpit-adjacent POV only
Constant forward velocity
Micro-jitter always on
Whip-pans triggered by threats
Roll / yaw / pitch never settle
Camera reacts before the brain does.
Foreground elements constantly crossing frame
Camera often too close, partially occluded
Lens breathing during acceleration
Lenses (mixed):
24mm wide for canyon runs
35mm for pursuit chaos
50mm tele for compression during dives

PHYSICS RULES
Debris has real mass and momentum
Everything has mass and speed
Near-miss shockwaves buffet the camera
Explosions push air, water, debris outward
Explosions displace smoke, dust, fighters
Wreckage does not vanish — it becomes obstacles
Missiles curve late, violently, unnaturally

No float.
No slow motion.
Momentum always wins.

Collision & Explosion Physics:
All impacts obey real momentum and mass dominance. High-velocity collisions exceed material limits and cause immediate structural failure. Lighter craft disintegrate on impact; larger structures suffer penetrative breaches followed by internal explosions and outward decompression. Explosions produce directional blast forces, triggering secondary system failures (fuel, reactors, ammunition). Shields flicker and collapse under sustained fire. No clean separations, no cosmetic explosions, no harmless collisions. Debris has weight and momentum. Shockwaves visibly displace camera and environment.


